# Kandelo patch rationale (S18)
#
# Node can retain native byte spans after a JS wrapper is detached or
# collected. Stock external-buffer APIs cannot cover every engine-created or
# resizable allocation. Keep generic engine adoption, resize, detach and
# allocator operations; the bridge now owns the concrete shared lease and
# exactly-once release policy. The OS cannot manage JS buffer lifetimes.
# Lease/deleter code must stay resident until the last native owner retires.
#
# Source-only cleanup; not rebuilt or behavior-qualified. Retention remains
# subject to README.md: Future work: platform omissions.

